    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This essay won or received an honorable mention for The Boothe Prize for excellence in first-year writing. The Boothe Prize recognizes and rewards outstanding expository and argumentative writing by undergraduate students in first-year classes that satisfy the WR 1 requirement. In each award-winning essay, student writers demonstrate clarity of argument, excellent integration of research-based evidence, and compelling prose style.\r\nThis essay argues that the genre of the food video is rapidly changing the culinary landscape: through harnessing the power of social media, it invites an unprecedentedly enormous audience to reconsider the many assumptions surrounding home cooking as something difficult and time-consuming. Dynamic, inclusive, interactive, and ubiquitous, it is the twenty-first century’s rejoinder to a long history of cookbook discourse that has, at times, insisted on glorifying the exclusivity of haute cuisine and propagating traditional gender roles in the kitchen.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
